        "kind": "math",
        "text": "Prior/update/interval: A recent-Q4 persistence model uses the 2023-Q4 and 2024-Q4 average, (1,637 + 1,660) / 2 = 1,648.5 thousand, based on the 11-quarter 2023-Q1\u20132025-Q3 historical sample. Apply the sole adjustment component, -13.5 thousand for softer 2025 total gross gains, giving 1,635.0. Because this is a flow series, dispersion is computed from all 11 listed quarterly values themselves: sample sigma = 40.7 thousand. The normal 80% half-width is 1.28*sigma = 1.28*40.7 = 52.1 thousand, implying 1,635 \u00b1 52, or final bounds of 1,583 to 1,687 thousand."
